{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794296580,"nonce":"+q1pTnUZEJXPhnR6fZ8rarquGQ8=","title":"A primitive missing from a loaded HDLL aborts with a message that names neither the library nor the function","message":"GitHub issue #1 (hoseyjoe): after the startup line '2 missing: ui@hlp_ui_choose_dir, sdl@hlp_win_get_display_scale' the program ended with 'Error: GetProcAddress failed: The specified procedure could not be found. (os error 127)'. The error is libloading's text from NativeLibraryManager's symbol lookup, propagated with no context, so it reads as a loader or Windows fault.\n\nCause in that report: the program was built against a newer sdl and ui than the sdl.hdll and ui.hdll loaded (win_get_display_scale is in HashLink master's SDL3 sdl.c). Stock HashLink also refuses to start there (module.c: Failed to load function %s@%s), so the behavior is parity; only the message is poor.\n\nFix: name the library and function, say the program was built against an HDLL that has it, keep the loader text. Checked with cargo check -p ash --release only; no unit test, since the lookup needs a real HDLL.","files":null}]}